---
title: Chewy Sugar Cookies
image: https://thetoastykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/soft-sugar-cookies-stack-01-1-1024x1536.jpg
source: https://youtu.be/hgxRfVqcr7o?si=XxIUpiBQF6wIDtpj 
---

Mix @butter{100%g}(unsalted, melted or close to, just shy of 1 stick) with @sugar{120%g}(.5cup + 2tbsp) and @vanilla{1%tsp} until well combined.

Add in @egg yolks{2} and mix until just combined.

Add @all-purpose flour{140%g}(1 cup + 1 tbsp), @salt{1/2%tsp}, @baking powder{3/4%tsp}, and @baking soda{1/2%tsp}. Mix just until the flour disappears.

> If you like the large shaped sprinkles, add some in here.

Shake dough into smaller balls on a #cookie sheet{}.

> If you're more partial to sparkling sugar, sprinkle on top here.

Cool dough in the fridge for about ~{30%minutes}.

Bake for ~{10-12%minutes} at 350°F.

Let rest for a few minutes, then move to the wire rack and let it finish cooling.